---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About - The Whetstone"
  description="What The Whetstone does: structural logic auditing for written arguments. 26 fallacy patterns, Toulmin decomposition, counterargument generation, citation audit, and evidence-weighted likelihood."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <main>

    <!-- Hero with side rail -->
    <section class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12 sm:pt-24 pb-16 sm:pb-20">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12 items-start">

        <!-- Main hero column -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-8">
          <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-gray-900 leading-[1.1] mb-6">
            See the structure<br class="hidden sm:block" /> behind every argument.
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-gray-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-8 sm:mb-10">
            The Whetstone analyses the reasoning in any text - what's claimed, what evidence is offered,
            where the logic breaks down, and the strongest opposing case the writer didn't engage with.
            Not a verdict on who's right. A structural view of how the argument works.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 sm:gap-4">
            <a href="/reader" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 sm:px-6 py-3 bg-indigo-600 text-white text-sm font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-indigo-700 transition-colors">
              Try the audit - free
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
            </a>
            <a href="/creator/studio" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 sm:px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors">
              Open Creator Studio
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Side rail with trust strip -->
        <aside class="lg:col-span-4 space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-5">
            <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-3">By the numbers</p>
            <dl class="space-y-3">
              <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-xs text-gray-500">Reasoning patterns</dt>
                <dd class="font-serif text-xl text-gray-900">26</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-xs text-gray-500">Analytical lenses</dt>
                <dd class="font-serif text-xl text-gray-900">11</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-xs text-gray-500">Papers searchable</dt>
                <dd class="font-serif text-xl text-gray-900">200M+</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 p-5">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-800 mb-1">Privacy-first</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-emerald-700 leading-relaxed">
              No analytics, no tracking, no advertising. Audit text is processed and discarded - never stored.
            </p>
          </div>
        </aside>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Feature grid - 3 columns on lg+ -->
    <section class="border-t border-gray-200 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20">
        <h2 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-8">What the engine analyses</h2>

        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-0 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
          <div class="p-6 border-b lg:border-b-0 sm:border-r border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">🔬</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Argument structure</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              Toulmin decomposition - claim, grounds, warrant, weakest link. The skeleton of the argument, stripped of rhetoric.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 border-b lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">⚠️</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">26 reasoning patterns</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              From Post Hoc to Motte-and-Bailey, Selection Bias to Genetic Fallacy. Verbatim quotes, severity, confidence.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 border-b border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">⚔️</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Counterarguments</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              The 2-3 strongest objections a thoughtful opponent would deploy - each with its own Toulmin structure.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 sm:border-r border-b lg:border-b-0 border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">📎</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Citation audit</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              Every cited URL fetched and checked - does the source actually support the claim it's cited for?
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 lg:border-r border-b lg:border-b-0 border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">🧭</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Philosophical commitments</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              The ethical, epistemic, and political framework the argument operates within - made visible.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="text-2xl mb-3">📊</p>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Evidence-weighted likelihood</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
              For empirical claims, we search 200M+ academic papers and assess scientific consensus.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Two-product split -->
    <section class="border-t border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 lg:gap-8">

          <a href="/reader" class="group block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 sm:p-8 hover:border-indigo-300 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-500 mb-3">Reader</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl sm:text-2xl text-gray-900 group-hover:text-indigo-700 transition-colors mb-3">
              Audit any argument
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Paste text or a URL. The engine maps the structure, flags reasoning issues, and shows you the argument's bones. Free - no account required.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-600 group-hover:text-indigo-800">
              Open the Reader →
            </p>
          </a>

          <a href="/creator" class="group block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-6 sm:p-8 hover:border-amber-300 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-600 mb-3">Creator</p>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl sm:text-2xl text-gray-900 group-hover:text-amber-700 transition-colors mb-3">
              Stress-test your writing
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
              Full audit suite, counterarguments, citation checking, revision tracking, and inline highlights. For students, journalists, and professional writers.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-600 group-hover:text-amber-800">
              Open Creator Studio →
            </p>
          </a>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Base>
